      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 828767393,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Judging from lines 3996 to 3999 below, probably still want to set out_tvb even if hf_id is < 0. I believe a few of the BER and PER functions use setting hf_id < 0 when they want to retrieve a value without adding it to the tree. So perhaps the if (hf_id >= 0) line should guard the `proto_tree_add_item` that uses `hf_id` but not these lines?",
